Channeling usually happens when your coffee isn't packed down firmly and evenly enough in the portafilter, or when the grounds aren't distributed properly. The main ways to prevent it are: make sure you're distributing the grounds evenly before tamping, then tamp down with firm, level pressure, and check that your tamp is level and flat. If it keeps happening, you might also need to check that your grind isn't too coarse, since finer grounds pack together better and resist water pushing through.